{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888572,"nonce":"AXsYxNQwGJxn799sG4JZxNvOOsY=","title":"The Investigator has no model provider decision, so no real Investigation can run","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0053 names Investigator, Investigation, Step and Finding but not which model API oto calls, how its key is stored, or which model each tier uses. `180a525` runs behind a fake model; nothing real can.\n\n**The demonstration.** No LLM client in `go.mod`.\n\n**Why it matters.** Every 0053 slice ships behind the fake until this is decided.\n\n**Where.** Decision recorded as an amendment to ADR 0053: provider and SDK, sealed credential storage (reuse the `channel_credentials` sealing pattern), default model per tier (a cheap model for classification, a stronger one for investigation), whether self-hosted model endpoints are in scope; then the real adapter behind `180a525`'s model port.\n\n**Scope.** small — a decision and one adapter.\n\n**Done when.** The owner has ruled; ADR 0053 is Accepted with that ruling; CONTEXT.md's \"anything AI — DEFERRED-POST-V1\" module-map line is superseded; the real adapter passes the same contract tests the fake does.\n\n**Blocked by.** `180a525`\n\n**Mode.** HITL — needs a human decision or review before it can be implemented. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}